#question(title: [$arcsin$], shrink: true)[
  Let $display(f(x) = 1/sqrt(1 + x))$.
  + Find a formula for its derivatives
    $display(f^((n)) (x))$.
  + Write its Maclaurin series at $0$. Call
    it $S(x)$.
     #v(0.2cm)
  + What is the radius of convergence of
    series $S(x)$?

     #[
       #set text(size: 12pt)
       #emph[Note:] Use without proof that
       $display(f(x) = S(x))$ inside the
       interval of convergence.
     ]
  + Use this result to write $h(x) = arcsin$
    as a power series centered at $0$.

     #[
       #set text(size: 12pt)
       #emph[Hint:] Compute
       $display(h' (x))$.
     ]
  + What is $display(h^((7)) (0))$?
]
